MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Phases_en-US
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en-US
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: af0630ccbb05103429116160dc0530b4, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 1
    m_Localized: Start the next stage to get the hints and information.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2
    m_Localized: In the image to the side you can see a eukaryotic cell, with its
      structures. The nucleus is the control center for cellular activities, it has
      a rounded shape, with several pores.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3
    m_Localized: 'In the space to the side you must form mRNA by adding the complementary
      nitrogenous bases, observing the DNA bases: Guanine with Cytosine, and Adenine
      with Thymine or Uracil.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 4
    m_Localized: 'Pay ATTENTION: Uracil is only inserted into RNA and is complementary
      to Adenine.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5
    m_Localized: 'Read the disc from the center to the periphery and find the amino
      acid corresponding to the triplet of bases in the mRNA, for example: AUG=Met.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6
    m_Localized: Carefully, read the text below to better understand the processing
      of the chosen protein. Pay attention to its function, as it will be important
      in the next mission!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7
    m_Localized: Answer the question below according to the correct destination of
      the protein you chose, that is, indicate whether it acts within the cell itself,
      whether it is released into the bloodstream and will act on organs, or on other
      specific cells.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8
    m_Localized: If you need help, click on the button with the protein name and
      make the correct association.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
